     Question

  The production support team of xFusionCorp Industries has deployed some of the latest monitoring tools to keep an eye on every service, application, etc. running on the systems. One of the monitoring systems reported about Apache service unavailability on one of the app servers in Stratos DC.

Identify the faulty app host and fix the issue. Make sure Apache service is up and running on all app hosts. They might not have hosted any code yet on these servers, so you don’t need to worry if Apache isn’t serving any pages. Just make sure the service is up and running. Also, make sure Apache is running on port 3004 on all app servers.

   Soultion
 1- Install the epel-release and ansible
     sudo yum install epel-release -y
     sudo yum install ansible -y
 2- Logn into each app server
     ssh user@host
 3- Confirm Apache is listenning on port 3004
    sudo netstat -tulnp | grep 3004
 4- stop the port and start httpd
    sudo systemctl stop < the port on which port 3004 is listed>
    sudo systemctl start httpd
 5-Disable the port use by 3004
    sudo systemctl disable <the name of the port used>
 6- Enable it
     sudo systemctl enable < port use>
  - Check firewall rules
     sudo iptables -L -n | grep 3004
  - command breakdown
     sudo iptables -I INPUT 1 -p tcp --dport 3004 -j ACCEPT
